{"Calling updateManyByCredentialId with an empty update object will result in an invalid Prisma update (no fields to SET), causing a runtime error that breaks the sync flow. If the goal is to bump SelectedCalendar.updatedAt, explicitly set it in the update data.": 0.9357941746711731, "sed -i '' is BSD/macOS-specific and will fail on GNU sed (common on Linux). Make the in-place edit portable across macOS/Linux.": 0.9562572240829468, "Throwing a plain Error will be converted to an INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR by tRPC, which is misleading for a not-found/unauthorized credential. Use TRPCError with an appropriate code so clients can handle it correctly.": 0.7903916239738464, "Hard-coding 'en-US' for the cache timestamp ignores the user's selected locale. Use the runtime locale so the date/time formatting matches the rest of the app.": 0.801368772983551, "The cache deletion mutation doesn't invalidate the connectedCalendars query, so the displayed cache status/timestamp can remain stale until a manual refresh. Add an onSettled handler similar to the disconnect mutation.": 0.9960981607437134, "dev:cron now uses npx tsx, but tsx is not listed as a dependency in this workspace or the repo root. This will trigger a network download or fail offline. Since ts-node is still a dependency, prefer keeping ts-node until tsx is added as a dependency.": 0.9340547323226929}